assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

Starting with vendor version 2026-10-01, `GET /products` returns results in pages: for "cable" it sent 5 items with `"total":7` and `"next_cursor":"5"`. The published spec already documents the `cursor` parameter. `search_products` only read the first page, so it silently dropped the last two matches. The fix makes the handler keep requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` and collecting items until `next_cursor` is empty. The old 2026-01-01 version always returns `next_cursor: null`, so the v1 fixtures send the same single request and give the same output. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and all other tests pass. The repro test now fails only with the expected UNMATCHED_REQUEST for `GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5`, which will clear once fiks re-records the call. Separately, the new recording also shows prices in cents (6900 where v1 had 69), which breaks the `items.price.range` rule. I did not change that here because it is outside this trace's scope.

